I see the issue now. In the `relocate` function, when `addend` is non-NULL (SHT_RELA case) and `addsub == 0`, the code does:

```c
if (addend)
  {
    value += *addend;
    if (addsub != 0)
      {
        // read section contents
      }
    switch (type)
      {
        case ELF_T_##NAME:
          if (addsub != 0)
            tmpbuf.Name += value * addsub;
          else
            tmpbuf.Name = value;
        break
      }
  }
```

When `addsub == 0`, it sets `tmpbuf.Name = value` without reading the section contents. That's fine because it's assigning the whole value.

But when `addend == NULL` (SHT_REL case), the code does:
```c
else
  {
    Elf_Data *d = gelf_xlatetom (relocated, &tmpdata, &rdata, ...);
    ...
    switch (type)
      {
        case ELF_T_##NAME:
          tmpbuf.Name += (GElf_##Name) value;
        break
      }
  }
```

Here, `gelf_xlatetom` reads the section data into `tmpbuf`. If the section data is valid, this should work. But what if `gelf_xlatetom` fails? The code checks `if (d == NULL) return DWFL_E_LIBELF;`, so that's handled.

Wait, but there's a subtle issue. The `tmpbuf` is a union. When `gelf_xlatetom` reads data into `tmpdata` (which points to `tmpbuf`), it fills the union with the section data. Then `tmpbuf.Name += value` reads the value and adds to it. This should be fine.

